spoz2 0.1

# INVOICING: a non-software example.  The "system" is the set of rules that
# govern every invoice a small company issues, whatever produces the invoice
# (a template, a script, an accounts package, a person).  It shows that
# SPOZ2 is not specific to code: anything with an implementation and an
# intent can have a .spoz2.
#
# Versions here are dates written as dotted versions (2020.07.15), because
# the rules change when the law or the contract changes, not when software
# ships.  The retired reduced-rate rule stays in the file: an invoice from
# August 2020 is still governed by it when an auditor reads it in 2026.

system invoicing
  Invoices issued by Acme Ltd to its customers, in any channel.  An invoice
  is a claim for payment; once issued it is never edited, only credited.

invariant sequential-numbers
  since 2019.04.01
  Invoice numbers are sequential with no gaps.  A cancelled invoice keeps its
  number and is reversed by a credit note; it is never deleted.

invariant vat-at-tax-point-rate
  since 2019.04.01
  VAT is charged at the rate in force on the tax point date, not the issue
  date or the payment date.

invariant hospitality-reduced-rate
  since 2020.07.15
  until 2022.04.01
  Hospitality supplies are charged at the temporary reduced rate: 5% until
  2021-09-30, then 12.5%.  Retired when the standard rate resumed on
  2022-04-01.  Invoices from that period remain correct at the reduced rate.

invariant terms-from-contract
  since 2021.01.01
  Payment terms are 30 days from the invoice date unless the customer's
  contract states otherwise; the contract wins.

invariant contract-currency
  since 2021.01.01
  Amounts are in the currency named in the customer's contract.  If the
  contract is silent, GBP.
